  "observations": [
    "Retained Run surface passes its session id to rSa, which observes selection and renders iSa; iSa offers Add to chat for nonblank selected text with a session id.",
    "The retained Run action normalizes the selection, creates a terminal-selection text attachment stub, and requests chat attachment. Mutation success clears action state and requests chat focus; it does not clear the xterm selection.",
    "The Run selection subscription and control are not conditioned on process running state. Setup gno has no Add-to-chat action.",
    "Current main already has generic TerminalHost selection-to-chat support and a guarded WorkspaceView callback. PanelStrip passes that callback and chat id only to TerminalHost, not ScriptsPanel.",
    "Current Run ScriptOutput has no selection subscription, target-chat prop or Add-to-chat action. The same output component serves Setup and Spotlight; those roles must not gain the Run action by default."
  ],
